  "question": {
    "text": "The ionization enthalpies of Li and Na are 520 kJ <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and 495 kJ <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively. The energy required to convert all the atoms present in 70 mg of Li vapours and 230 mg of sodium vapours of their respective gaseous cations respectively are"
  },
